<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan October M2 money supply up 8.45 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan October M2 money supply up 8.45 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's broadest money supply measure, M2, grew an annual 8.45 percent in October 1996, below the state's 9-14 percent growth target as well as September's 8.69 percent rise, the central bank said on Monday.  </p>
<p>			   Oct 1996	   Sept 1996</p>
<p> M2 ANNUAL RATE	   +8.45		 +8.69</p>
<p> M1B ANNUAL RATE	  +5.51		 +4.67</p>
<p> M1A ANNUAL RATE	  +1.89		 +1.42</p>
<p>NOTE: M1A is cash, checking accounts and passbook deposits. M1B is M1A plus savings accounts. M2 is M1B plus quasi-money.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
